sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client · POST /bff/checkout
    participant R as FedGQL Router
    participant K as checkout subgraph · orchestrator
    participant CT as cart service · REST
    participant I as inventory service · REST
    participant P as payments service · REST
    C->>R: mutation SubmitCheckout(input: cartId, paymentMethodId, shippingAddress)
    R->>K: submitCheckout(input)
    Note over K: saga / process coordinator — a GQL subgraph must not call another GQL subgraph, so steps call the services' REST APIs (internal HTTP), not the router
    K->>CT: 1. GET /carts/{cartId} — lines + totalAmount
    CT-->>K: Cart (JSON)
    K->>I: 2. POST /inventory/reservations per line (sku, storeId, quantity, reservationId = order id)
    I-->>K: InventoryReservation (RESERVED / availableToSell)
    Note over K: 3. create a pending Order
    K->>P: 4. POST /payments (amount, currency, paymentMethodId, referenceId = order id)
    P-->>K: PaymentTransaction (SUCCESS / DECLINED)
    K->>CT: 5. DELETE /carts/{cartId}/items — clear the cart
    CT-->>K: Cart (empty)
    Note over K: on failure after a write, compensate (refund / release reservations / restore the cart) and return success false
    K-->>R: CheckoutResult { success, order, errors }
    R-->>C: { data: { submitCheckout } } — Order status and payment transaction
